# 9. Kubernetes doesn't have this problem

Inside Kubernetes, each service can still listen on:

```text
3000
```

because each Pod has its own network namespace.

Your Helm values remain:

```yaml
services:

  user:
    name: user-service
    port: 3000

  product:
    name: product-service
    port: 3000

  order:
    name: order-service
    port: 3000
```

and Kubernetes Services expose:

```yaml
service:
  type: ClusterIP
  port: 80
```

Therefore:

```text
                Kubernetes

user-service:80 ──────► user Pod:3000

product-service:80 ───► product Pod:3000

order-service:80 ─────► order Pod:3000
```

Order service gets:

```yaml
env:
  USER_SERVICE_URL: http://user-service:80
  PRODUCT_SERVICE_URL: http://product-service:80
```

So the **pnpm monorepo doesn't change your Kubernetes architecture**.

