# 10. Docker becomes interesting with the monorepo

Instead of having completely independent npm projects, each Dockerfile can build from the monorepo root.

For example:

```text
ecommerce-nodejs/
├── apps/
│   ├── user-service/
│   ├── product-service/
│   └── order-service/
├── packages/
├── package.json
├── pnpm-workspace.yaml
└── pnpm-lock.yaml
```

A Dockerfile for `user-service` can be:

```dockerfile
FROM node:22-alpine

WORKDIR /app

RUN corepack enable

COPY package.json pnpm-workspace.yaml pnpm-lock.yaml ./

COPY apps/user-service/package.json ./apps/user-service/package.json

RUN pnpm install --filter user-service --prod

COPY apps/user-service ./apps/user-service

WORKDIR /app/apps/user-service

EXPOSE 3000

CMD ["pnpm", "start"]
```

Build from the **monorepo root**:

```bash
docker build \
  -f apps/user-service/Dockerfile \
  -t user-service:1.0 .
```

Notice the final `.`.

That's important because Docker needs access to:

```text
package.json
pnpm-workspace.yaml
pnpm-lock.yaml
apps/
packages/
```

